<!--
  Apex Weather mark: a sun rising over the Apex Maps chevron.

  The ridge is the lower chevron of the Apex Maps A-sharp glyph, unchanged, at the scale and
  translate that glyph has always had. The upper chevron is gone; a sun stands where its peak was,
  because the icon opens a weather app and an arrow says nothing about weather. What is left of the
  family resemblance is the ridge and the palette — amber and cool blue on night sky.

  The rays are not decoration. Without them the disc and the chevron read as head and shoulders once
  Android flattens them to one colour for a themed icon. See ic_launcher_monochrome.xml.
-->
